--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
Rigid6 buoy with a clamped finite-EI cable and a rod pinned to the buoy (test deck)
-- examples/buoy_clamped_cable.dat with a 7.8 m arm rod pinned to Body1 (Body1Pinned) and a 6 s
-- run. The body's junction group then has nine coordinates (six of the body, three of the pin),
-- and the clamped cable's finite-difference Jacobian columns, kept across steps, span all nine.
